but is expected to have type Polynomial ℤ".  The unique well-typed reading
of "reduce the coefficients of `f : Polynomial ℤ_[p]` into `ZMod p`" is
`Polynomial.map PadicInt.toZMod f`: a ring hom `ℤ_[p] →+* ZMod p` is unique
(its image is the prime field generated by 1, its kernel a maximal ideal =
the unique maximal ideal `pℤ_[p]`, and the induced map `F_p → F_p` is the
identity), and `PadicInt.toZMod` is that hom — also the standing corpus
spelling of the mod-p reduction (O2aOrder1.lean; cited as the convention in
Locality.lean).  No other token differs from the display.  NOTE: the same
adjustment will be forced on III-S1b (`sq_not_dvd_reduction_of_disc_unit`)
and on the `hsq` row of `cu2t_readForcing`, which share this spelling.
